        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Early in 1825 someone began to knit this item of fine silk, but never completed the project. Eighty-nine stitches are on the very thin needles, still attached to the ball of silk yarn the knitter was using. It is 11 centimetres wide and was probably intended to be a purse. To knit with such thin needles and fine silk would have been quite time-consuming, but the finished texture is very beautiful.\n\nThe knitting came to the Museum in a cardboard envelope, on which was written: ‘My dear sister’s work, as she left it the last time she did any. She died 29th December 1825’."@en , "Knitting sample, four knitting needles, cardboard knitting folder and Valentine card.\n\nSample of unfinished knitting on needles in green silk yarn, in a cardboard folder with an enclosed card, possibly a Valentine."@en , "Knitted silk sample, steel knitting needles, cardboard knitting folder and Valentine card, England, ca. 1825"@en ;
